choose a slow, torturous death when a loaded shotgun was readily available beneath his bed. They also took issue with the way Stacey portrayed David as an alcoholic. According to those who knew him well, he wasn't a regular drinker and only consumed alcohol on special occasions. From the outset, suspicions lingered that there was more to the story. Not only did the antifreeze bottle and glass in David's bedroom appear unusually clean, almost like they'd been staged, there was also the question of why it's. turkey baster containing anti-freeze was found in the kitchen bin. And why did Stacey call for a welfare check from her office instead of going to the house to check on David first? Investigators were

